+/* ---- resolves kept on the GPU ------------------------------------------- */
+/*
+ * A title resolving its supersampled scene into VRAM every frame and drawing
+ * the result to the screen with one full-screen pass used to cost a whole
+ * readback of the scene, its store into guest memory, and a re-hash, decode and
+ * upload of the same pixels as a texture -- with the GPU idle while the frame
+ * thread waited for it. Instead the resolved pixels are copied on the GPU into a
+ * colour target the engine keeps for that guest range (eng_resolve), and a
+ * texture unit naming exactly that image samples the target. Guest memory gets
+ * the pixels only when something else reads those bytes through the engine: a
+ * texture of another shape or format, a 2D transfer, a surface store. What it
+ * cannot see is the CPU reading them directly; RSX_ENGINE_GPU_RESOLVE=0 keeps
+ * the old store of every resolve for a title that does.
